# will_refuses — a will proposes nothing off its way, and nothing at all where it cannot be done
#
# Two wills held in the Test Field, pinned to the Test Berry Bush:
#   lockpicking — its lock is the Test Door off the yard. The bush is no step of that way, so thinking
#     on it proposes nothing: it says what it wants and leaves the bush be, without naming the way,
#     which the rewrite took for a resolve with no act behind it.
#   pugilitas — wants to come to blows, and the people are in the yard. Thinking on the bush proposes
#     nothing, and names the man it would strike by his label, never the verb's bare "him": said of
#     somebody else, "attack him" names the wrong man.
#   butchery — wants to cut a carcass, and nothing in the test location has died: no path exists in
#     this place at all, so observing refuses the focus and thinking proposes nothing, both saying
#     that only leaving offers it.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-mm lockpicking,butchery,pugilitas --grant-item hairpin --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Field" --period dawn

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
observe "Test Berry Bush"
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

advance 12 180
expect-state will "will lockpicking steps=2"
expect-state will "will butchery steps=none"

# Not this way: no action, and the way named.
click keyword bush
choose 0
choose lockpicking
advance 12 180
expect I want to pick a lock: to unlock
expect but that does nothing for it, and I leave it be
expect-not to get there

# Not this way, with a person at the end of it: named, not pronounced.
click keyword bush
choose 0
choose pugilitas
advance 12 180
expect : to attack the
expect-not attack him

# Not in this place: the focus is refused, and why.
click keyword bush
choose 1
choose butchery
advance 12 180
expect have to leave it
quit
